export default "Name: Aman Bansal. Location: Bengaluru, India. Role: full-stack developer (Node.js, React). Email: amanabbansal@gmail.com. GitHub: https://github.com/Aman21253. LinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/aman-bansal1/.\nEducation: B.Tech in Computer Science, Arya Institute of Engineering and Technology, Jaipur, 2022-2026, CGPA 7.7/10. Solved 180+ DSA problems on LeetCode. Certifications: NPTEL C Programming (IIT Kharagpur), Infosys Springboard Full Stack Development.\nEXPERIENCE (five internships since 2024):\n- Software Engineer Intern at Xoxoday, Bengaluru (Jul 2026 – Present):\n  * Build backend features and REST APIs on a Node.js, Express and MongoDB microservice architecture for internal enterprise tools, working in an Agile team.\n  * Built the citation-generation module for the award nomination workflow.\n  * Built a Q&A feature integrated with Google Workspace for surveys.\n  * Use Kafka for event-driven communication between services, Redis for caching and GraphQL for efficient data fetching.\n  * Cut rollback time from 40s to 12s by removing redundant repeated API calls, and manage Kubernetes deployments with Devtron.\n- Backend Engineer Intern at Velocity Software Solutions, Remote (Jan – Jun 2026):\n  * Designed and implemented Node.js microservices and REST APIs for Bitebox, a multi-role food delivery platform, on MongoDB and MySQL.\n  * Built the order lifecycle and coupon modules.\n  * Built the payout module that settles earnings for restaurants and delivery partners.\n  * Implemented real-time delivery tracking from live location updates, with role-based access for customers, restaurants and delivery partners.\n  * Managed Docker-based deployments and improved CI/CD pipelines.\n- SDE Intern at Celetel, Noida (Sep – Nov 2025):\n  * Built production REST APIs for e-commerce features.\n  * Designed WhatsApp Business (WABA) analytics dashboards to monitor campaign metrics.\n  * Learned how production APIs are reviewed, tested and released, including acting on code review feedback.\n  * Learned to shape API responses around what dashboards and campaign reports need.\n- Full Stack Developer Intern at Satvacart, Remote (Jan – Mar 2025):\n  * Improved application performance by 5% with targeted backend optimizations.\n  * Learned to find slow spots by measuring first, then changing code and queries.\n  * Learned how the front end and back end of a full-stack app fit together, from API contract to screen.\n  * Learned to work in a remote team: Git branching, pull requests and clear written updates.\n- Backend Engineer Intern at STAGE, Noida (Apr – Aug 2024):\n  * Completed structured backend training in Node.js, REST API development and database fundamentals.\n  * Built practice REST APIs and exercises under mentor guidance.\n  * Learned how an Express project is organized: routes, controllers, middleware and error handling.\n  * Learned the basics of database design and querying, and how APIs read and write data.\n  * Learned to improve code from mentor reviews and to test endpoints with Postman.\nPROJECTS:\n- Bitebox: A Swiggy-style food delivery platform built as independent services for orders, live tracking and payouts. Tech: Node.js, Express, MongoDB, MySQL, Docker, REST APIs. One order lifecycle shared by three roles: customers place orders, restaurants prepare them and delivery partners deliver them. Independent services for orders, tracking and payouts that talk to each other over REST. Role-based access so customers, restaurants and delivery partners each see only their own tools. Live location-based tracking of every order on its way to the customer. A coupon module for discounts and a payout module that settles earnings for restaurants and delivery partners. MongoDB and MySQL used together across the services, deployed with Docker and an improved CI/CD pipeline.\n- Patent Workflow & AI Search: Full-text and faceted search over large patent datasets, with a recommendation module for related patents. Tech: Python, Django, Apache Solr, REST APIs. Indexed large patent datasets in Apache Solr for fast full-text and faceted search. Exposed search through REST APIs consumed by the workflow UI. Built a recommendation module that surfaces related patents.\nGITHUB REPOSITORIES:\n- GlobeFlicker (JavaScript): GlobeFlicker is a stay-booking platform inspired by Airbnb. Hosts list places with photos, prices and locations, and travellers browse the listings and open each one for full details. The pages are rendered on the server with EJS templates, styled with CSS and powered by a JavaScript back end. Tech: JavaScript, EJS, CSS. \n- OptBharat (JavaScript): A freelance project that shows Indian-made alternatives next to well-known foreign products. Visitors can compare the options and choose products made in India, which helps local makers get noticed. Tech: JavaScript. \n- RFP Management System (JavaScript): A vendor and RFP (Request for Proposal) management system. Teams publish an RFP, vendors respond with proposals, and the proposals are compared before a vendor is chosen. The back end is built with Django REST Framework. Tech: Django REST Framework, Python, JavaScript. Vendor management: register vendors and keep their profiles and contact details in one place. RFP creation: define requirements, deadlines and evaluation criteria for each request. Proposal submission: vendors respond with their pricing and terms. Comparison and selection: review proposals side by side and award the work. Status tracking from draft to closed, available through REST APIs.\n- Book Management System (Python): A complete book management system built with Django. It uses access control lists (ACL), so each user can only view, add, edit or delete what their permissions allow. Tech: Python, Django, ACL. Add, view, update and delete books. Access control lists decide which user can perform which action. Built on Django models, views and authentication.\n- Bitebox (JavaScript): A Swiggy-style food delivery platform built as independent services for orders, live tracking and payouts, used by customers, restaurants and delivery partners. Tech: Node.js, Express, MongoDB, MySQL, Docker, REST APIs. One order lifecycle shared by three roles: customers place orders, restaurants prepare them and delivery partners deliver them. Independent services that talk to each other over REST. Role-based access, so each role sees only its own tools. Live location-based tracking of every order. Coupon and payout modules, with MongoDB and MySQL used together.\n- Main Project (EJS): An online store web app. Customers register, log in, browse the shop, add items to a cart and see their bill, while the shop owner uses a separate admin page to add products with images, prices and discounts. Tech: Node.js, Express, MongoDB, Mongoose, EJS, JWT, bcrypt, Multer, Tailwind CSS. Registration and login with bcrypt-hashed passwords and a JWT kept in a cookie. The shop and cart pages are for logged-in users only. The shop page lists every product stored in MongoDB, with its price and discount. Add to cart and remove from cart, saved on the customer’s account. The cart page totals price minus discount for each item and adds a flat 20 charge to the bill. An owner admin page creates products with an uploaded image (Multer), price, discount and display colours. The owner account can be created only in development mode, and only once. Success and error messages are shown with flash messages, and the pages are rendered with EJS.\nSKILLS:\n- Backend: Node.js, Express, NestJS, Django, Django REST Framework, REST APIs, GraphQL, JWT, Microservices\n- Data and messaging: MongoDB, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka, RabbitMQ\n- Frontend: React, Redux, HTML & CSS\n- Delivery: Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Nginx, Git\n- Languages: JavaScript, TypeScript, Java, Python, SQL";
